From: ud34d025a513c07fc at groups.google.com (Winston Chang)
Date: Mon, 27 Jan 2014 16:26:45 +0000
Subject: "branch" renamed to "layer"
Message-ID: <3lHVM2BjpHo.GVBDEyJyngoJ@ggvis.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/ggvis/c/3lHVM2BjpHo/m/GVBDEyJyngoJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi everyone -

Just a heads up - "branch" and other related functions have been renamed to "layer". Hopefully this will be a more intuitive interface for users.

For example, this is the old way of adding a smooth line:
  ggvis(mtcars, props(x = ~wt, y = ~mpg)) +
    mark_symbol() +
    branch_smooth(props(stroke := "red"))

And this is the new way:
  ggvis(mtcars, props(x = ~wt, y = ~mpg)) +
    mark_symbol() +
    layer_smooth(props(stroke := "red"))

-Winston

